feat(security): first-class ApiToken entity + MCP auth switch

The v0.2 MCP server accepted the same short-lived JWT bearer
tokens the REST API issues, which forced AI clients to log in
and out like a Web user. v0.3 replaces that path with a
first-class long-lived API token:

- New domain entity ApiToken (id, userId, name, hashedSecret,
  secretPrefix, scopes, expiresAt, lastUsedAt, revokedAt,
  revokedBy, revokedReason) + value objects ApiTokenName and
  ApiTokenScopes (with a Scope enum and parser). The cleartext
  secret is generated via RandomNumberGenerator, base64url
  encoded, and SHA-256 hashed before persistence; the prefix is
  the first 8 chars of the cleartext for UI display.

- Application layer: IApiTokenRepository (FindByHashedSecretAsync,
  ListForUserAsync) + IApiTokenService (Issue/Validate/Revoke/
  ListForUser) + IssueApiTokenCommand + RevokeApiTokenCommand +
  ListApiTokensForUserQuery + DTOs.

- Infrastructure: ApiTokenRepository (EF Core with
  AsAsyncEnumerable for the value-object filter, matching the
  existing LabelRepository pattern) + ApiTokenService
  implementation + ApiTokenConfiguration (RowVersion with
  IsConcurrencyToken + HasDefaultValue(0u), HashedSecret unique
  index, Scopes serialized as ;-joined TEXT).

- New migration IssueApiTokens (api_tokens table, 17 columns,
  2 indexes, FK-less by design since ApiToken is its own aggregate
  root scoped to a single user).

- REST API: POST/GET/DELETE under /api/security/api-tokens. Issue
  returns the cleartext secret exactly once; subsequent lists
  return only the prefix.

- MCP: ApiTokenAuthenticationHandler replaces the v0.2 JWT-bearer
  handler. The handler reads the bearer, calls
  IApiTokenService.ValidateAsync, and produces a ClaimsPrincipal
  with NameIdentifier (user id), token_id, and one scope claim
  per granted scope. McpCurrentUser now exposes Scopes alongside
  the existing Roles.

- Removed unused stubs: ApiTokenAuthenticationOptions.cs,
  ICurrentUserResolver.cs, McpCurrentUserResolver.cs, and the old
  JwtBearerAuthenticationHandler.cs.

- Tests: 7 new unit tests on the domain entity (issue/revoke/
  expiry/idempotency/validation) and 4 new integration tests on
  the full HTTP lifecycle (issue + list + revoke roundtrip,
  cross-user revoke rejected, anonymous issue rejected, empty
  name rejected with 400).

Verified: 187 unit + 20 integration tests green. The full
vertical smoke (register -> workspace -> board -> list ->
card -> comment -> label -> issue-and-use API token) still
works on real SQLite.
